sections.code:
ROSTER NOTATION  -  list the members between braces
  A = {2, 3, 5, 7}
  B = {red, green, blue}
  E = {}                 the empty set, also written ∅

SET-BUILDER NOTATION  -  state the membership rule instead
  A = { x ∈ Z : x is prime and x < 10 }
  read:  the set of integers x such that x is prime and x < 10
  same set as the roster above:  {2, 3, 5, 7}

MEMBERSHIP  -  one question, one yes-or-no answer
  3 ∈ A      true    3 is one of the listed members
  4 ∉ A      true    4 is not listed
  {3} ∈ A    false   A contains the number 3, not the one-element set {3}

ORDER AND REPETITION CARRY NO INFORMATION
  {1, 2, 2, 3} = {3, 2, 1}      both name the same three members

Congruence mod 3 on Z:   a ~ b   iff   3 | (a - b)

  reflexive     a - a = 0 and 3 | 0                          yes
  symmetric     if a - b = 3k then b - a = 3(-k)             yes
  transitive    if a - b = 3j and b - c = 3k then
                a - c = (a-b) + (b-c) = 3(j+k)               yes

So ~ is an equivalence relation.  Its classes, shown inside {0,...,8}:

  [0] = {0, 3, 6}
  [1] = {1, 4, 7}
  [2] = {2, 5, 8}

  disjoint:  no number appears in two of them
  covering:  every number appears in one of them
  =>         the classes form a PARTITION of {0,...,8}

Names are not classes:  [0] = [3] = [6].  One block, three labels.
Going the other way, the partition { {0,3,6}, {1,4,7}, {2,5,8} }
rebuilds ~ exactly:  a ~ b iff a and b sit in the same block.
